+# November 4 assistance and search supplement — publication review
+
+This export appends the reviewed four-part supplement to the preceding public master. Its addition is byte-for-byte identical to the canonical reviewed text; all earlier public master bytes remain intact. This publication does not repeat or upgrade the originating source checks. The original 175 master IDs and 481 owning findings remain unchanged and overlapping.
+
+| Requested point | Preserved result and unresolved test |
+| --- | --- |
+| Saudi-linked assistance | Evidence-based jurisdictional findings, preliminary scope, rejected video inferences, unknown call content and trial-stage motive questions retained. Underlying financial, telephone, employment and assistance exhibits remain comparison targets. |
+| Competing FBI assessment | Both the affirmative no-knowing-conspiracy assessment and prosecution-evidence conclusion retained. The correction to approximately 60 interviews in its stated 2007–2016 scope remains beside the earlier count. Exhibit-by-exhibit comparison, referenced serials and original interview inventory remain TODOs. |
+| Informant access | Executive restriction, recruitment-protection rationale, agency cooperation and later counsel/immunity position remain distinct. Original requests, refusals, service instructions and concurrence records remain TODOs; motive is not inferred from the restriction alone. |
+| August 2001 search | Criminal-agent exclusion, deletion of one copy, disputed legal consultation and routine priority retained with dissemination distinctions, organizational explanations and the negative plot-specific intelligence finding. Original emails, clearance, legal advice and assignment records remain TODOs. |
+| Citations and scope | Every primary URL and locator, every contrary-findings paragraph and all four discriminating-test blocks are preserved in the exact addition. No new original evidence, present court-status review, numerical probability, physical finding or completed request is claimed. |
+| Privacy and authority | Only the research addition, public checklist, additive metadata and verification changes are exported. No lawsuit material, private correspondence, raw chat/source inventories, private filesystem locators, contacts, credentials or original media are included. Original sources and earlier editions remain preserved. |
+| Verification | Earlier 2,228 checks remain enforced against the exact preceding public master; new checks cover the append, five new anchors, four qualified rechecks, citations, limitations, links and complete payload hashes. Negative controls test changes to both the predecessor and addition, including attempted rehashing. Passing checks establish preservation and publication, not historical truth or causation. |
+| Revision and identity | [Exact text changes](../../TEXT-CHANGES.diff) compare this update with the immediately preceding public commit recorded in UPDATE.json. The diff and its containing payload manifest are excluded from their own diff. Commit author, committer and authenticated push must be AveLyra with the account's noreply metadata. No main-branch merge, history rewrite, deletion, outreach, request submission or fee is part of publication. |
+
+Source-check limitations remain explicit in the addition: the earlier court PDF check used selected pages; the FBI check used the released extracted text; the informant appendix recheck did not obtain a fresh full PDF/page-image review; and no original search emails, legal advice or recipient records were acquired. These limitations remain open after publication.
